following which would leave a bishop hanging and not taken...} 15... Bf5 16.
Rhe1 Nb4 17. d6 Bxc2+ 18. Ka1 cxd6 19. Qxb4 Bxd1 20. Bxd1 d5 21. Qxe7 Rxe7 22.
Nxd5 Rd7 23. Nxf4 Rad8 {- also incorrect - see below} 24. Ba4) 16. Qc4 Bf5 17.
Rhe1 Nb4 18. d6 Bxc2+ 19. Ka1 cxd6 20. Qxb4 Bxd1 21. Bxd1 d5 22. Qxe7 Rxe7 23.
Nxd5 Rd7 24. Nxe3 Re8 (24... Rad8 25. Ba4 {is the erroneous finish given in
BCM 1910, p540.}) 25. Ba4 {Sources: Northampton Mercury, 30 Sept 1910;
Northern Whig, 13 July 1911 (with the score as supplied by O'Hanlon himself)}
1-0

